  "articleBody": "It can be frustrating when you see other businesses getting cited by AI overviews and answer engines, but your content seems invisible. You're probably wondering what gives! A lot of businesses face this, especially with the shift from traditional keyword-based search to conversational AI. The truth is, AI systems look for very specific signals that traditional SEO often misses.\n\nFirst off, AI crawlers prioritize structured data, meaning your content needs to be neatly organized with schema markup like JSON-LD. This isn't just about throwing a basic FAQPage schema on your site; it's about dense, nested schema that tells AI exactly what your business does and answers real questions. Most older websites or those using heavy CMS themes like WordPress, Wix, or Squarespace often struggle here because they don't provide the clean, static HTML and rich schema AI systems love. These themes can also slow down AI crawlers, making it harder for them to even find your valuable information.\n\nAnother big factor is the type of content you're creating. Traditional SEO often focuses on broad keywords, but AI Visibility Solutions, for instance, focuses on answering the *exact* questions people are asking. This means going beyond simple FAQs to address those nuanced queries found on platforms like Quora, Reddit, and even your own Google Search Console's ",
